{"term":"urge","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0692bb45efdc9db619","definition":"A strong desire to do something.","example":"After seeing the advert for a soft drink, I had a sudden urge to buy a bottle.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["hunger","yearning","ache","appetency","appetite","craving","hankering","hunger","impulse","itch","jones","letch","lickerish","longing","lust","pining","thirst","urge","yearning","yen"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee7b116a1e85b61b63","definition":"To press; to push; to drive; to impel; to force onward.","example":"Lo hapless Tydeus, whose ill-fated hand / Had slain his brother, leaves his native land, / And seized with horror in the shades of night, / Through the thick deserts headlong urged his flight[…]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["animate","encourage","impel","stimulate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overurge","reurge","urge on"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fae0d2e83693ab3612","definition":"To put mental pressure on; to ply with motives, arguments, persuasion, or importunity.","example":"My boss urged me to reconsider my decision to leave the company, even offering a pay rise.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["instigate","abet","actuate","goose","fuel","light a fire under","send","sting","bring about","cheer","draw","drive","encourage","egg on","engender","evoke","excite","foment","goad","grill","ignite","impel","incite","induce","inflame","instigate","invoke","lash","motive","motivate","move","obligate","oblige","push","promote","prompt","provoke","rouse","set off","spark off","spur","spur on","stimulate","stir","stir up","stoke","tempt","urge","whet","whip up"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overurge","reurge","urge on"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:36caee27ee4feb24ed","definition":"To provoke; to exasperate.","example":"Vrge not my fathers anger (Eglamoure) / But thinke vpon my griefe (a Ladies griefe) / And on the iuſtice of my flying hence, / To keepe me from a moſt vnholy match, / Which heauen and fortune ſtill rewards with plagues.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["agitate","strain","test","vex"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overurge","reurge","urge on"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d672fd24c45e2650e","definition":"To press hard upon; to follow closely.","example":"Man ? and for ever ? wretch ! what wouldst thou have ? / Heir urges heir, like wave impelling wave.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overurge","reurge","urge on"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cc386864d5797e7cdb","definition":"To present in an urgent manner; to insist upon.","example":"to urge an argument; to urge the necessity of a case","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overurge","reurge","urge on"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/urge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"